/-!
# S1830: the R'-level (G2) and (G3) of S1779, actually proved

S1825 reduces the Galois structure on the actual small cover category
S1809CoverCategory01 to the algebra-side pre-Galois data over

  R' = S1726CoordinateRing = F'[x,y]/(y^2 - x^3 - (61/64)x^2 + (125/64)x),

the coordinate ring of the punctured affine elliptic curve E' minus O.  The
two remaining algebra-side fields are

* S1779QuotientsMissing -- (G2): colimits of finite group actions in
  (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale R')^op (equivalently: the invariant subalgebra
  A^G of a finite etale R'-algebra under a finite group action is finite
  etale over R', and is the categorical quotient);
* S1779MonoMissing -- (G3): every monomorphism in
  (CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale R')^op is a coproduct injection, i.e. every
  epimorphism of finite etale R'-algebras splits as a product projection.

R' is a Dedekind domain and **not** a field, so the field-case arguments of
S1746/S1770 (subalgebras of finite etale algebras are finite etale) and of
S1771/S1785/S1811 (product-of-fields decomposition) do not apply.
Nevertheless both fields are proved here for an arbitrary commutative ring,
hence in particular for R', by genuinely different mechanisms.

## (G2): invariants under finite group actions

The general fixed-point theorem
FiniteEtaleFixedPointsGeneral.fixedPointSubalgebra_finiteEtale (already in
the tree, imported here) proves, for an arbitrary commutative ring R, a
finite etale R-algebra A with a finite group G acting by R-algebra
automorphisms, that A^G is finite etale over R.  Its mathematical proof is
Galois descent: split A by a finite faithfully flat etale cover T
(Algebra.IsFiniteSplit.exists_tensorProduct_of_etale, Mathlib), where the
fixed points are computed explicitly as functions on orbits of the induced
permutation action, and descend the finite-etale property along T/R.  No
invertibility of |G| and no field hypothesis is used.  This file constructs
the invariant object and the limit cone over the action diagram, and hence
the colimit in the opposite category, exactly as S1746 did over a field.

## (G3): epimorphisms split

For an arbitrary commutative ring R:

* every epimorphism f : B -> A of finite etale R-algebras is surjective.
  The pushout A (x)_B A is finite etale over R (S1779's tensor cocone),
  hence a legitimate test object; epimorphy forces the two tensor inclusions
  to agree, i.e. Algebra.IsEpi B A; since A is finite over B, Mathlib's
  Algebra.isEpi_iff_surjective_algebraMap_of_finite gives surjectivity.
* a surjective map of finite etale R-algebras splits: the kernel is an
  idempotent ideal (formal etaleness over B), hence finitely generated by an
  idempotent e (A is finitely presented over R and finite over B), and
  B ~= A x B/(1-e) with f the first projection.
* the resulting binary product fan is a limit in the full subcategory of
  finite etale algebras, so its opposite is the required binary coproduct
  cofan in (FiniteEtale R)^op.

This proves both S1779QuotientsMissing and S1779MonoMissing for R' (and
for every commutative ring), hence the unconditional algebra-side
PreGaloisCategory (FiniteEtale R')^op via S1779's terminal/pullback/
finite-coproduct fields.  The geometric fibre functor and the affine
equivalence are separate inputs and are not used here.

## Honest boundary

No sorry, admit, new axiom, Shrink, ULift or PUnit.  The axiom footprint is
audited at the end and is exactly propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.
-/

